<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand light. Sales confirmed for the week to date on 6300 cattle, mostly previously contracted or formulated cattle. The last established price was at $68.00 per cwt Friday, March 7. Tuesday bids $65.00-$66.00, asking $69.00-$70.00.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
